{{!--
  Site navigation. Sticky bar; the same five destinations and the same hrefs the
  Bootstrap 3 navbar carried.

  Desktop (lg+): each dropdown group opens on hover, on focus-within (so Tab alone
  reaches every sub-link) and when its chevron button reports aria-expanded="true".
  Mobile: one disclosure button toggles the panel, and the dropdowns are simply
  visible groups inside it — the chevron buttons are display:none there, so their
  aria state never lies about a menu that is already open. The toggle's icon and
  label swap (hamburger/Menu -> X/Close) purely off its own aria-expanded, via
  the group-aria-expanded: variant — no extra JS needed for that part.

  Behaviour lives in /js/site.js. Nothing else.
--}}
<nav class="border-b border-brand-900/40 bg-brand-800 text-sand-100" aria-label="Main">
